  "label": "Islamophobia Stereotype",
  "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that Muslims are inherently violent or associated with terrorism, which is a core component of Islamophobia. This stereotype is used to justify the warning in the text that 'they always blow up in your face' — implying that making jokes about Muslims will provoke violent retaliation. This is a harmful and inaccurate generalization that equates all Muslims with terrorism, which is a well-documented form of prejudice.",
